          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which of the following is the single strongest risk factor for developmental dys</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which of the following is the single strongest risk factor for developmental dysplasia of the hip?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Female sex</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Female sex increases DDH risk sixfold due to ligament laxity from circulating maternal oestrogens, but this is not the strongest individual risk factor.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Breech presentation</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Breech presentation restricts hip flexion and abduction in utero, raising DDH risk twentyfold — the highest of any single risk factor.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Positive family history (affected first-degree relative)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A positive family history increases risk tenfold through a likely polygenic mechanism, but breech presentation confers an even greater relative risk.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Reduced amniotic fluid (oligohydramnios)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Oligohydramnios restricts fetal movement and is a recognised risk factor, but its relative risk is substantially lower than breech presentation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Not quite. While all of these are recognised risk factors, breech presentation carries the highest relative risk at twentyfold, compared with sixfold for female sex and tenfold for family history."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! Breech presentation is the strongest single risk factor, raising DDH risk twentyfold by restricting normal hip movement during fetal development."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
